// title: Top 10 users with the most ips used to succesfully sign in · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: 
// tables: 
// purpose: Collect the top 10 user with the most IP used to succefully sign in to a tenant. This query displays the 10 users that have used the most IP addresses so sign in. False positives can be a VPN that changes IP addresses, which results in a high number of IPs used to sign in.
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Azure%20Active%20Directory/Top10UsersWithTheMostSignInIPsUsed.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
AADSignInEventsBeta
| summarize IPsUsed = make_set(IPAddress), locations = make_set(Country) by AccountObjectId
| extend CountIP = array_length(IPsUsed)
| project-reorder CountIP
| top 10 by CountIP
